  "cleanText": "Solution home \n\t\tCapium 365\n\t\tCapium 365 (Accountant)\n\n### Capium 365: Sources\n\n\t\t\tPrint\n\n\tModified on: Fri, 28 Feb, 2025 at  3:09 PM\n\nThe Sources feature within Capium 365 allows individuals and sole traders to track different streams of income efficiently. By categorising earnings into distinct sources, users can organise and report income accurately, ensuring compliance with financial and tax regulations.\n\nNote: The Sources tab is only available for individuals and sole traders. If you are using a different entity type, this section will not be visible. Instead, transactions can be posted directly into the Bookkeeping module.\n\nAdding a Source\n\n### Navigation: Capium 365 Module > Select a Client (Individual or Sole Trader) > Click on Sources > Click on the \"+ Add Source\" button\n\n### Click here to go directly to sources\n\n### Please see below the steps of filling in a source\n\nFill in the required details:Source Type: Choose from UK Property, Foreign Property, or Self-employed business.\nID: Enter a unique identifier for the source.\nBusiness ID: Provide the associated business ID.\nTrading Name: Specify the trading name.\nAccounting Type: Select the applicable accounting type.\nCommencement Date: Enter the start date for this source.\nAddress Details: Include Postcode, House/Flat No, Street Name, City, County, and Country.\nNon-FHL: If applicable, select this checkbox for non-furnished holiday lettings.\n\nClick Save or Save and Exit to confirm the entry.\n\n###  \n\n### Understanding the Sources Dashboard\n\nNavigation: Capium 365 > Find the client you want to investigate > Click Go to 365 > Click Sources > The Sources dashboard provides a snapshot of income streams and profitability\n\nOverall Sources Profitability: Displays total income, expenses, and net profit.\nSource List:Source Code: A unique identifier for each source.\nSource Name: The name associated with the income stream.\nType: Categorises the source (e.g., Foreign Property, UK Property).\nIncome & Expenses: Shows financial activity linked to each source.\nProfit: Calculates net earnings per source.\nIs Primary: Allows users to mark a primary income source.\n\n### Reviewing Posted Data for a Source\n\n### Navigation: Capium 365 Module > Select a Client (Individual or Sole Trader) > Click on Source > Once a source has been added and transactions are posted, you can review the associated data.\n\nPlease click here to go to the sources tab\n\n### Subheadings in sources\n\nNavigation: Capium 365 > Sources > Click into the source you want to investigate > Please see below different sub headings:\n\nProfit & Loss Summary: View an overview of income, expenses, and net profit.\nIncome: Displays all income transactions linked to the source.\nExpenses: Lists all expense records associated with the source.\nDetails: Provides comprehensive source information.\nHistory: Logs modifications and updates made to the source.\n\nClick here to go to sources\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDid you find it helpful?\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tYes\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNo\n\nSend feedback\tSorry we couldn't be helpful. Help us improve this article with your feedback.",
